From 4ff7829724c30d29ce11a96672274a832099a9ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:58:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 47/65] MAS local: never check for updates

Not for upstream: it is the opposite of the upstream design.

At every start vl.c calls android_checkForUpdates(), which ran a
SystemClockUpdateChecker on a worker thread. At most every 4 hours per
emulator version (timestamp in emu-update-last-check.ini in the user
directory) it fetched
https://dl.google.com/android/repository/repository2-3.xml with libcurl,
with the installation id, OS, host bitness, emulator and core version in
the query string. No metrics option turns it off.

This build never checks for updates: upgrades come from whoever
distributed it. android_checkForUpdates() now only logs one line saying
so, and DataLoader::load() returns nothing instead of fetching the XML,
so the Help page of the extended controls (the only other user) shows
"Unavailable" as the latest version instead of making the request.

Usage metrics and crash reports are covered by "MAS local: never upload
usage metrics" and "MAS local: never upload crash reports".

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: Id0fdc2ef49ee8818f3a9333030d36a8751c475a6
